\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Per-expert normalized trust \(\bar  \alpha _k\) (mean \(\pm \) std over \(200\) seeds) for each expert mixture and training variant; experts are labeled reliable (R), noisy (N), or adversarial (A). Stabilized initialization with detached \(w_k\) assigns high, low-variance trust to the reliable majority (\(\bar  \alpha _k\approx 0.94\)) while driving the minority noisy expert toward zero and the adversarial expert negative (\(\bar  \alpha _k\approx -0.73\) under 3R1A), whereas the standard random-initialization variant leaves \(\bar  \alpha _k\) near zero on average with large seed-to-seed variance. The Consensus variant (random initialization plus the reward anchor) recovers the same sign pattern (reliable positive, noisy near zero, adversarial negative) because it regularizes the reward rather than the trust; the separation is weaker and noisier than under stabilized initialization owing to the softer reward signal. Under 1R3A the adversarial majority captures high trust while the lone reliable expert is suppressed, the trust-level signature of the flipped branch.}}{13}{figure.caption.17}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:synthetic-branch}{{2}{13}{Per-expert normalized trust \(\bar \alpha _k\) (mean \(\pm \) std over \(200\) seeds) for each expert mixture and training variant; experts are labeled reliable (R), noisy (N), or adversarial (A). Stabilized initialization with detached \(w_k\) assigns high, low-variance trust to the reliable majority (\(\bar \alpha _k\approx 0.94\)) while driving the minority noisy expert toward zero and the adversarial expert negative (\(\bar \alpha _k\approx -0.73\) under 3R1A), whereas the standard random-initialization variant leaves \(\bar \alpha _k\) near zero on average with large seed-to-seed variance. The Consensus variant (random initialization plus the reward anchor) recovers the same sign pattern (reliable positive, noisy near zero, adversarial negative) because it regularizes the reward rather than the trust; the separation is weaker and noisier than under stabilized initialization owing to the softer reward signal. Under 1R3A the adversarial majority captures high trust while the lone reliable expert is suppressed, the trust-level signature of the flipped branch}{figure.caption.17}{}}
